# TaskManager — Product Overview

A role-based task manager: **admins** set up people and projects, **project leads** drive assigned work, **members** see only what they are assigned.

## Roles (what each person does)

| Role | After login | Can do |
|---|---|---|
| **Admin** | Admin dashboard | Users (CRUD, roles), projects (CRUD, archive, members), tags, create/edit/assign tasks, comments |
| **Project lead** | Assigned projects | Update **progress** and **status** on tasks in those projects; mark a task **completed**; view assigned tasks |
| **Member** | My tasks | View assigned tasks only (read-only). No project list, no progress edits |

Register always creates a **member**. Only an admin can raise role.

## The assignment chain (the product)

```
Admin
  → creates project
  → assigns project lead + members  (project membership)
  → creates task + assigns people   (task assignment → notification)
Project lead
  → opens that project
  → updates progress / status
  → dashboard % refreshes from assignments
  → marks task completed
Member
  → notification + My tasks
  → opens task (read-only)
```

- **Project membership** = who belongs to the project (lead + members).
- **Task assignment** = who is on a specific task. Assignee gets a **task assigned** notification. Lead/admin can also assign themselves.
- **Progress** lives on the assignment (`0–100`). Project dashboard % = average of those scores (completed tasks count as 100).
- **Status** is `todo` | `in_progress` | `done`. Leads set todo/in progress; **completed** is a separate confirm step after a save.

## What the UI must make obvious

1. Admin: create project → add team → create task → assign people.
2. Lead: open assigned project → pick a task → progress or status → save → see dashboard update → optionally mark completed.
3. Member: assigned tasks list → open details. Nothing else.

Keep copy short. One primary action per screen. Don't dump admin, lead, and member controls on the same view.

## Stack (as of the apps/ split)

- **Frontend:** React + Vite + TypeScript in `apps/frontend` (`/api` proxied to FastAPI).
- **Backend:** FastAPI + SQLAlchemy 2 async + PostgreSQL in `apps/backend`.
- **Auth:** JWT (`python-jose`); login is OAuth2 password form (`username` = email).
- **AI:** NVIDIA NIM optional (`NVIDIA_API_KEY`) for task title + project context → description.
- **Frontend must not** call NVIDIA or the DB. Backend must not import React.

## Constraints

- Do not invent extra roles.
- Members never edit progress, status, or assignments.
- Leads only see/update projects they are a member of.
- Assigning a user to a task creates a notification — keep that side effect.
- Prefer the existing `apps/frontend/src/api` and `apps/backend/app` layers over new parallel clients.
